### United States House of Representatives, District 11 @federal-united-states-house-of-representatives-district-11
> San Francisco
contest, partisan
note: Open seat after Nancy Pelosi's retirement. Two Democrats advanced from the
  June top-two primary.

+ Scott Wiener (Democratic)
- Connie Chan (Democratic)

Scott Wiener is the most accomplished legislator in the State Senate. He has
single-handedly passed some of the most important housing legislation in
California, and he is more responsible than anyone for the state's wholesale
rethinking of housing policy.

Chan, by contrast, has been one of the worst, most anti-urban members of the San
Francisco Board of Supervisors. Her main accomplishments include opposing bike
lanes, wanting to reopen the Great Highway to cars, and a general hostility to
the idea of urban density. Her candidacy is only viable at all because of some
stupid Pelosi-Wiener beef, which is not a reason to send her to Congress. She
fucking sucks. Do not vote for her.

