region

#### Regional Measures @bay-area-regional-measures

##### Regional Measure RTM @bay-area-regional-measure-rtm
> Regional transit sales tax
measure
placed by: Multi-county signature petition under SB 63
yes: Enacts a 14-year sales tax of 1% in San Francisco and 0.5% in Alameda,
  Contra Costa, San Mateo, and Santa Clara counties, raising about $980 million
  a year, mainly to prevent service cuts at BART, Muni, Caltrain, AC Transit,
  VTA, and SamTrans.
supporters: Connect Bay Area Transit coalition, Scott Wiener, Jesse Arreguín,
  Nancy Pelosi, SPUR, Seamless Bay Area, Transform, SEIU 1021, the transit
  agencies, GrowSF
opponents: Committee for Affordable Bay Area Transit, Contra Costa Taxpayers
  Association, Debora Allen, Steve Glazer, Quentin Kopp, Mercury News and Daily
  Post editorial boards
note: Each county's share goes to its own agencies. San Francisco's goes mostly
  to Muni and BART, Alameda's about 65% to BART, Santa Clara's mostly to VTA and
  Caltrain, and San Mateo's to Caltrain and SamTrans. Needs 50%+1 across all
  five counties combined to pass.
vote: yes

