#### Oakland Ballot Measures @oakland-oakland-ballot-measures

##### Measure EE @oakland-measure-ee
> Strong mayor charter amendment
measure
placed by: City Council on a 4 to 4 vote, with Mayor Lee breaking the tie
yes: Replaces Oakland's hybrid mayor and city administrator system with a
  strong-mayor system. The mayor becomes chief executive with a legislative veto
  and a line-item budget veto, overridable by six of eight councilmembers, and
  loses the council tie-breaking vote. The council gains confirmation power over
  key department heads, subpoena power, and a full-time role.
supporters: Mayor Barbara Lee, Council President Kevin Jenkins, former mayor
  Libby Schaaf, Empower Oakland, San Francisco Foundation
opponents: Councilmembers Zac Unger, Janani Ramachandran, Noel Gallo, Ken
  Houston, former councilmember Loren Taylor, Supervisor Nate Miley, Oakland
  NAACP
note: The City Auditor estimates a first-year implementation cost of $2 million
  to $2.6 million.
vote: undecided

##### Measure FF @oakland-measure-ff
> End the transfer tax foreclosure exemption
measure
placed by: City Council, unanimous
yes: Starting in 2027, removes the real property transfer tax exemption for most
  transfers through foreclosure, keeping exemptions for individuals acquiring
  small residential property and for community banks, generating an estimated $4
  million to $13 million a year.
supporters: Councilmember Charlene Wang, SPUR, Empower Oakland
vote: undecided

