#### Palo Alto Ballot Measure @palo-alto-palo-alto-ballot-measure

##### Measure J @palo-alto-measure-j
> Half-cent sales tax for Cubberley
measure
placed by: City Council, unanimous
yes: Raises Palo Alto's sales tax by 0.5% with no sunset, about $15.6 million a
  year as a general tax, which the Council says it intends to use to buy PAUSD's
  seven acres of Cubberley Community Center and modernize it.
supporters: All five council members, the PAUSD board, teachers' union, Joe
  Simitian, League of Women Voters of Palo Alto, Palo Alto Forward
opponents: Former mayor Lydia Kou, Silicon Valley Taxpayers Association, Mercury
  News and Daily Post editorial boards
note: Because it is a general tax, nothing legally binds the money to Cubberley.
  Combined with RTM, Palo Alto's sales tax would exceed 10%.
vote: undecided

