#### San Mateo Ballot Measures @san-mateo-san-mateo-ballot-measures
> No special district contest reaches a city ballot this year. Peninsula Health
> Care District and the Harbor District seats were uncontested, and the city is
> outside the open space district.

##### Measure H @san-mateo-measure-h
> Quarter-cent city sales tax increase
measure
placed by: City Council, 4 to 0
yes: Raises San Mateo's local sales tax from 0.25% to 0.50%, about $7 million a
  year for general city services, with no sunset, annual audits, and groceries
  and prescriptions exempt.
supporters: Former police chief Susan Manheimer, former councilmember Richard
  Hedges, Parks and Recreation chair Sabrina Ocampo, San Mateo Daily Journal
opponents: Council candidate Taso Zografos and two co-signers, no organized
  committee
note: The city projects a structural deficit of about $17 million.
vote: undecided

##### Measure F @san-mateo-measure-f
> City charter cleanup
measure
placed by: City Council
yes: Updates the City Charter to formally recognize district elections and
  redistricting, extends the window to fill council vacancies from 30 to 60
  days, modernizes meeting and notice rules, and removes council approval of the
  Finance Director appointment.
supporters: Councilmember Danielle Cwirko-Godycki, Deputy Mayor Nicole
  Fernandez, former councilmember Richard Hedges, San Mateo Daily Journal
vote: undecided

##### Measure W @san-mateo-measure-w
> San Mateo-Foster City schools bond, $498 million
measure
placed by: San Mateo-Foster City School District board
yes: Authorizes $498 million in general obligation bonds, about $29 per $100,000
  of assessed value, to replace windowless classrooms, roofs, and windows,
  upgrade STEM and career classrooms and emergency systems, and build roughly 80
  workforce housing units for staff at the Knolls campus.
supporters: SMFC Education Foundation, PTA Council, Supervisor Noelia Corzo,
  Councilmember Rob Newsom Jr., San Mateo Daily Journal
opponents: Thomas Weissmiller and co-signers, who cite the existing Measures T
  and X on the same tax bill
note: Needs 55% to pass.
vote: undecided

##### Measure V @san-mateo-measure-v
> Community college district bond, $848 million
measure
placed by: San Mateo County Community College District board
yes: Authorizes $848 million in bonds, about $18 per $100,000 of assessed value,
  to repair and build science, engineering, trades, and career classrooms and
  fix roofs, plumbing, and electrical systems at College of San Mateo, Cañada
  College, and Skyline College, keeping the current tax rate rather than raising
  it.
supporters: SMCCD Federation of Teachers, county firefighters, San Mateo County
  Central Labor Council, Silicon Valley Community Foundation
opponents: Silicon Valley Taxpayers Association and co-signers, who note it is
  the district's fifth bond since 2001 and cite the Galatolo bond scandal
note: Needs 55% to pass.
vote: undecided

##### Measure U @san-mateo-measure-u
> Independent redistricting commission
measure
placed by: Board of Supervisors
yes: Creates an independent commission to draw and adopt the five supervisorial
  district boundaries after each census, replacing the current system where the
  Board of Supervisors adopts maps on the advice of an advisory committee.
supporters: Supervisors Jackie Speier, Noelia Corzo, Lisa Gauthier, League of
  Women Voters chapters
vote: undecided

##### Measure J @san-mateo-measure-j
> Time to fill county vacancies
measure
placed by: Board of Supervisors
yes: Extends from 30 to 60 days the time the Board of Supervisors has to appoint
  a replacement or call a special election when a non-supervisor elected county
  office becomes vacant, and requires a noticed public meeting before any
  appointment.
supporters: Board of Supervisors and the Charter Review Committee
vote: none

##### Measure L @san-mateo-measure-l
> Charter preamble on extreme weather
measure
placed by: Board of Supervisors
yes: Adds a paragraph to the County Charter preamble declaring long-term
  resilience to fire, flood, heat, drought, and sea level rise a county
  priority.
supporters: Board of Supervisors and the Charter Review Committee
vote: yes

##### Measure AA @san-mateo-measure-aa
> Charter preamble affirming rights
measure
placed by: Board of Supervisors
yes: Adds a paragraph to the County Charter preamble affirming the county's
  commitment to the dignity, civil rights, and equal protection of all
  residents. No other changes.
supporters: Board of Supervisors and the Charter Review Committee
vote: yes
